<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anne of Forez</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1358–1417</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Anne Dauphine</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anne of Forez was the heiress of the County of Forez in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. Her marriage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-ii-duke-of-bourbon">Louis II, Duke of Bourbon</a>, in 1371 brought Forez into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a> lands. It remained with the Bourbon family until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-i">Francis I</a> confiscated the possessions of Constable <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-iii-of-spain">Charles of Bourbon</a> and united Forez with the crown in 1531.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anne-of-forez.jpg" alt="Anne of Forez" width="320" height="679" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anne_d%27Auvergne_BnF_Fran%C3%A7ais_22297_fol._15.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
